            {
              "about": "The form of a practice",
              "decided": "Each practice opens with one or two sentences on what its condition gives the users and the method it comes from. Then it lists its items in the order the maker takes them: each decision with its question and its criterion, each step, and the check from the users' side. Each item says when the maker takes it: while it settles the work's decisions, or while it makes the deliverable. An item's ID is its condition's ID and its place, such as N6.2. A role ends by naming the IDs of the items it took, so that a check finds one skipped, while what the item made stays the evaluator's to judge.",
              "by": "user"
            }
          ]
        },
