        {
          "id": "N3",
          "good": false,
          "decisions": [
            {
              "about": "The slices",
              "decided": "Seven slices, in this order. First, a role held to the commands its rules name, laid by lay.py write from a proposal. It carries S2 and S4. Second, lay.py print, which shows the steps as they'll read and refuses a proposal that can't stand. It carries S1. Third, a result only from the result script, and the starts in the order of the routes from a run's call to its end. It carries S3 and S5. Fourth, each step held in its order by its trace, each item that a role's result must name, and the other types of rule the steps call for. It carries S4. Fifth, a start with only the text the plugin gives, a role resumed with the main conversation's grounds and the person's words, and a route that waits until the person's command. It carries S3. Sixth, a run picked up at the run port. It carries S6. Seventh, lay.py up. It carries S7.",
              "by": "reasoning"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "N4",
          "good": false,
          "decisions": []
        },
        {
          "id": "N5",
          "good": false,
          "decisions": []
        },
        {
          "id": "N6",
          "good": false,
          "decisions": []
        },
        {
          "id": "N7",
          "good": false,
          "decisions": [
            {
              "about": "The tools that find the missing tests",
              "decided": "check.sh fails on any line or branch of Lane's code that the tests don't run, measured by coverage with the copies that lay.py write lays counted as the source, and on any mutant of cosmic-ray under which every test passes. hypothesis tries the guard over any call. All three come with the test-quality group and run on CI's newest Python. mutmut can't serve: it counts a mutant tested only when a test calls the code under the module name of its path from the root, and Lane's code runs as domain and __main__, as Claude Code runs it. fest skips mutants it takes for untested, some of them run.",
              "by": "user"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "N8",
          "good": false,
          "decisions": []
        }
